Description: take ownership through the BObjectList template parameter
 V\OS carries object ownership as the second template parameter of
 BObjectList (template<class T, bool Owning>) and only offers the
 itemsPerBlock constructor, so the legacy BObjectList(20, true) form does
 not compile. Owning the records is what upstream asks for, so declare
 BObjectList<Queryable, true> and construct with (20).
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: vendor
Last-Update: 2026-10-23
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/

--- a/source/querywindow.h
+++ b/source/querywindow.h
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
 			private:
 				BMessenger m_reply_to;
 				Query* m_query;
-				BObjectList<Queryable> m_records;
+				BObjectList<Queryable, true> m_records;
 		};
 
 		Worker* m_worker;
--- a/source/querywindow.cpp
+++ b/source/querywindow.cpp
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@
 	BLooper(),
 	m_query(query),
 	m_reply_to(reply_to),
-	m_records(20, true)
+	m_records(20)
 {
 	PRINT(("QueryWindow::Worker::Worker(Query*, BMessenger)\n"));
 }
